Jitsi Meet on FenrirOS
======================

This package installs the web files in /usr/share/jitsi-meet and nothing else:
no web server site, no configuration, no domain, no accounts. A working Jitsi
installation also needs:

  - a web server (nginx) serving /usr/share/jitsi-meet, with TLS
    (sample: /usr/share/doc/jitsi-meet/nginx-jitsi-meet.conf.example);
  - Prosody (package prosody, plus jitsi-meet-prosody, the plugins) as the
    XMPP server, configured for your domain
    (/usr/share/doc/jitsi-meet-prosody/prosody.cfg.lua-jvb.example);
  - Jicofo and Jitsi Videobridge (packages jicofo and jitsi-videobridge, if
    present in the repository: they are the conference focus and the media
    server; without the videobridge nothing but one-to-one calls works);
  - optionally coturn for clients behind strict NATs (package coturn).

/etc/jitsi/meet/<your domain>-config.js is your copy of
/usr/share/doc/jitsi-meet/config.js.example (set hosts.domain, hosts.muc,
bosh/websocket). The nginx sample includes it by path. Open 443/tcp and
10000/udp (the videobridge).
